    "Pinned 0x5CE640 loads codes and samples from stack +0xC/+0x10 into ESI/EDI, reads a byte through ESI and writes a word through EDI advancing by two; existing general.h already declares unsigned char* and short* parameters.",
    "Limit production edits to this signature and the two int-to-pointer conversions. Preserve loops, unchecked paths, state order, original mappings, historical claims and TRIED evidence. Reconstructed catalogue decorations do not establish original types.",
    "Compile the modified TU under a coordinator compiler lease and update the explicit symbol using the native writer with the observed emitted symbol; never guess a decorated symbol or edit ORIGINAL markers.",
    "Remove host-only signature rewriting so actual pointer-typed code is tested; retain all decoder controls and mutants. Native storage controls must select the current annotated symbol and retain layout, initializer and reference checks.",
    "All 94 general.cpp identities are measurement/preservation scope. Require scoped comparison, fresh compile/link, claims/reference continuity and coordinator-reviewed integration; this does not establish full game or automatic acceptance."
  ],
